x86_64-linux  One cxx1-only name, `_ZN1GD1Ev`: the complete-object form of the destructor the compiler writes for `G`, which has a member with a destructor of its own. clang emits only the base-object D2 form on this target and calls that, where cxx1 emits both - identical bodies for a class with no virtual base, and the same fact move-constructor.nonames and reference-temporary-lifetime.nonames record. Every other name agrees, and x86_64-windows and arm64-darwin agree with clang name for name - which for this case is the half that matters, its subject being a Microsoft unwind record.
